A||||10||nette||1987 - 5spd VS Automatic||||1||
Z||000000||nette||11-16-2001||12:55 PM||||Need some quick advice please.  Looking into buying another Fiero, an 87 GT.  I have a couple good leads, one is a 5spd, one is an automatic.  Any pros/cons or advantages/disadvantages to either one (besides of course personal preference of shifting or not)?  Any and all help would be greatly appreciated.<P>nette||||reg||1
Z||000001||BlackStang95||11-16-2001||01:07 PM||||Stick is always quicker if youre a half decent driver.  About a 1/2 second or so to 60 and nearly a full second in the 1/4.||||reg||4
Z||000002||nette||11-16-2001||01:14 PM||||I am a good driver, especially with a stick.  I have usually always driven automatics if given the choice, however my 87 coupe is a stick and I love driving it.  I guess if there is no strong advice AGAINST the automatic then I won't think twice about it.  I like to go fast but I am not going to be racing so one second slower isn't going to make any difference to me.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||11-16-2001||01:21 PM||||It's not just that sticks are just faster, they are WAY more fun to drive also. I'd never buy an automatic fiero again. Only con to the sticks is they need clutches and other work done to them every once and a while. Autos almost never have anything go wrong with them.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||11-16-2001||02:16 PM||||In Montana, you are not stuck in bumper to bumper traffic and you have lots of open space. Nothing worse that stop and go traffic with a manual transmission.  The 5 speed runs at lower rpms at highway speed so better gas milage.  You can hold the car in gear with the manual for better performance. (Unless you want to shift the auto)  I have one of each, but I like my 87 with the 5 speed more as a drivers car.||||reg||1
Z||000005||NEPTUNE||11-16-2001||04:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Master_Sushi:<BR><B>It's not just that sticks are just faster, they are WAY more fun to drive also. I'd never buy an automatic fiero again. Only con to the sticks is they need clutches and other work done to them every once and a while. Autos almost never have anything go wrong with them.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Automatics burn way more gas- i ger 18 city (if traffics not toobad) 24.7 highway with 87 auto. Unless you have to fight heavy traffic get the 5 s[pd.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||11-16-2001||04:41 PM||||Sticks are fun, but not necessarily quicker ( <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/pat.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/pat.htm</A>  ).  The 3spd will definitely burn more fuel- and run the engine at a higher RPM on the highway, thus creating more engine noise.  The Auto is more durable, but it really isn't an issue (other than clutch replacement) unless you're planning on running huge horsepower. Also the auto is better for launching from a standstill... less/no chance of breaking loose the rear tires (even my balding tires stick- unless the road is wet or I'm cornering).<P>I'd agree- If you regularily get stuck in traffic, go with the auto.  If not- then the stick.  Either way, drive the car & enjoy it!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||85ZainoGT||11-17-2001||01:15 AM||||gimney chritmas, you think a stick is a FULL second faster??? no no no... not a chance, unless your ABSOLUTELY amazing at shifting and you power shift.. but really, if you get an automatic, just get a higher stall TC and youwill beat any manual off the line and in the long run, autos shift faster  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I do like sticks though, but gets tiring after a while, especially if you have a girl with you..  but thats beyond the point... <P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 Gold GT 2.8L<BR>All the options :)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SigPic2222.jpg"> <BR>NEW pics are coming SOON hopefully... geez!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula||11-17-2001||08:48 AM||||my auto breaks the tires loose||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fformula88||11-17-2001||09:40 AM||||If you do a lot of commuting driving, you'd probably be more satisied with the auto.  If you use the car more for spirited driving, go with the stick!  <P>I agree that the manuals are 1/2-1 sec faster too!  I don't have a problem launching the 4-spd in the 85 SE.  If you feather the clutch out at the right pace I can get a much faster launch than can in the auto in my Formula, and I can nail that 1-2 shift very quickly, and THAT is a real kick in the pants!  IMO the manual is a half second to full second faster!  However, I love my auto just the same.<P>Automatic transmissions certainly can fast too!  My uncle has a '79 Trans Am with a rebuilt engine bored and stroked to 455 cubes hooked up to an auto!  That things can lay some serious twin stripes on the road, and it can also toast nearly any car you can come across.  Next spring he's takin it to the track to get some real times!  It rocks!!||||reg||1
Z||000010||Philphine||11-17-2001||09:50 AM||||everything i've got drivable for the past 6 years has been a stick but sometimes (like when i hurt my foot) an auto would have been nice to have. if you plan to keep the coupe maybe an auto wouldn't be too bad. have you got any other drivers (truck, sedan) with stick or auto to help make the decision? ||||reg||1
